    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, i'll look into getting a soft brush. it's just that even when i'm cleaning, it feels so... unrewarding? like i'll clean out one corner and then i'll turn around and i swear i see a new little bit of string or a scrap of paper just sitting there where it shouldn't be. it's almost like these tiny little things are just popping up out of nowhere to mess with me. does that happen a lot? like, is it normal for a collection to feel like it's actually trying to be difficult or uncooperative?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
